kwin-ctm-monitor (0.1.12-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix testCustomCtmLifecycle: the hardware test-and-commit inside
    tryKmsColorOffloading only runs once the pipeline has an active,
    presented frame, so a bare queueChanges/applyQueuedChanges call in this
    harness legitimately stays at Testing rather than reaching Active
    (matches the same gap noted by testModeset's own QSKIP). The 0.1.11-1
    build predates this fix and fails during its KWin test run.

 -- Charles Jones <charles.jones@valencesoftware.io>  Mon, 06 Jul 2026 17:30:00 -0400

kwin-ctm-monitor (0.1.11-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Stop restoring a persisted CTM automatically during output setup; a
    matrix is only ever applied interactively against a running session.
  * Remove the frame-presented gating (AwaitingFrame/DrmOutputCtmFeedback):
    it fired immediately during plasmalogin's compositor-reused handoff and
    protected nothing.
  * Set CustomSdrCtmStatus::Active synchronously right after a successful
    hardware test, matching how every other color decision in this function
    already works.
  * Add kwinctmctl-restore, an autostart script that reapplies the last
    confirmed matrix a few seconds after a Wayland session starts, using the
    same interactive path that has always worked reliably.
  * Rev the downstream KWin packages to ctm5.

 -- Charles Jones <charles.jones@valencesoftware.io>  Mon, 06 Jul 2026 17:00:00 -0400

